// "Spillway": a quiet figure and a wall of sound, at 84, in E minor, thirty-two bars, about a
// minute and a half. Original music, written here, by Claude for Ryan. Nothing of any recording
// or score is quoted.
//
// It is the first piece written from the wrela-music skill's taste sheet (references/taste.md):
// fourteen tracks Ryan named, the moments in them he loves, and what was found to be happening
// at each. This piece is a test of that sheet, so it says which of its devices it uses.
//
// The concept. Water held, then let go. Hypnotic, mournful, enormous. E natural minor, 84 BPM,
// straight sixteenths. Two chords in the verses, E minor and C major with its seventh, two bars
// each; three in the choruses, C, D and E minor, a bar each, with no dominant chord anywhere
// (device 5). The one bold thing is the size of the step between the two.
//
// The bed is a figure (device 4): sixteen plucked sixteenths to a bar in groups of three,
// three, three, three, two and two. Each group is a top note and then B and E under it, the
// same two every time; only the top note moves, one to a bar: B, A, G, F♯. It stops on F♯, the
// second step, and goes round. An echo follows it a dotted eighth behind.
//
// The tune finishes what the figure starts. The figure walks down B, A, G, F♯ and never
// arrives; the chorus sings B, A, G, F♯ and E. Each of its notes is sung and then touched
// again just before the next, long then short (device 6), with the note above leaned on in
// between: B with C over it, the same a step lower, then G, F♯, and home to E a push early.
// Its second half starts the same, leaps to the high E, its one highest note, and comes down.
//
//   C            D            Em           Em
//   B––b C––b    A––a B––a    G––g F♯––e   E––– · · ·
//   C            D            C            D            | Em (the verse)
//   B––b C––b    A––a B––a    E'––e' D–––  C––c B––––   | B–
//
// The chorus never ends on its own home chord. The first time, the tune stops on B over the D
// chord and holds it across the bar line; everything else cuts off on the bar line, with no
// fill; and the verse's E minor arrives under the B, with the figure taking the B up as its
// own top note. The cut is the resolution (device 3). The second time the tune walks on down
// the scale and its last step, F♯ to E, lands as the last E minor does.
//
// What is the same, made heavy (device 2): in the choruses the low wall and the bass strike the
// figure's own grouping, three, three, three, three, two, two, on each chord's root.
//
// The palette, by role:
//   the figure     a plucked patch, clean, with its echo: the bed of the verses
//   foundation     verses: a soft bass drum on one, a rim, a shaker, and the bass's upper layer
//                  held very softly. Choruses: a low bass drum every dotted quarter, the snare on
//                  three (half time), a ride on every beat, the sub and the round bass together
//   the wall       two driven layers to either side: roots and fifths low, striking; the chord's
//                  three notes higher, held
//   held           a pad voiced to sing: E and B under the verses, the chords high over the
//                  choruses; a cello, a viola and a violin from the second verse
//   lead           a sung lead; a second voice a third over it in the second half of each
//                  chorus only (device 7); the violin an octave over it in the second chorus
//   the twinkle    the electric piano's bell, high and soft, a few notes a bar in the verses
//                  (device 9)
//
// The form, with the level each part should have:
//
// - bars 1-8, the first verse (about 18 dB under full scale by bar): the figure alone for two
//   bars; then the soft bass, the bass drum on one; from bar 5 the rim, the shaker, the voices
//   on E and B, the twinkle. In bar 8 the figure stops halfway and the lead sings four notes up
//   the scale alone (device 1).
// - bars 9-16, the first chorus (about 11): everything, on the downbeat, with no fill before
//   it. A fill on the toms in the tune's rest (bar 12). It cuts on the bar line.
// - bars 17-22, the second verse (about 18): the figure again, with the cello bowing its top
//   notes an octave down. The strings swell through the last two bars; everything else stops
//   halfway through bar 22, and the lead sings its four notes over the strings alone.
// - bars 23-30, the second chorus (about 11): with the strings, the violin over the tune.
// - bars 31-32: E minor. The tune's last note, the strings and the voices hold; the figure
//   comes back alone, and its top note is E at last.
//
// Chosen from five kinds tried on paper for the tune: this one; a four-note motif said again
// over the next chord (too many leaps, loose from its chords); a chant on two neighbours and a
// fall (the nearest rival: kept as the hover inside this one); one long note a bar (no rhythm);
// a leap up from the low E and a long fall (the last two pieces' trick).
//
// What it can't do. The tracks it is modelled on are guitars and voices, and the engine has
// neither: the plucked patch stands for a clean guitar, the driven saws for an overdriven one,
// the sung lead and the pad for voices. A tempo that lifts a little into the chorus, as several
// of those tracks do, is not possible within one session either.
//
// No ear has heard it. Measured: by bar, the verses sit near -18 dB and the choruses near -11,
// a step of about 7 dB each way at every cut; scripts/feel.py raises no flags (no notes struck
// hard, a semitone sounding 12% of the time, nothing outside the key); the lead plays the tune
// as written.

use engine::bowed::{CELLO, VIOLA, VIOLIN, bowings}
use engine::drum::{Drum, HAT, KICK, RIM, SNARE}
use engine::pattern::{Feel, Pattern, pattern, struck, swung, tacet}
use engine::perform::{Mark, Performance, Taste, bar, perform}
use engine::score::{Meter, Score, meter, score}
use engine::session::{Master, Session, Strip, session}
use engine::synth::{LEAD, PAD, Patch, SUB}
use engine::tine::{SUITCASE, Tine}
use engine::tone::Shape

pub const TITLE: Text = "Spillway"
pub const TEMPO: f32 = 84.0
pub const BARS: u32 = 32

fn four() -> Meter {
    meter(beats: 4, unit: 4)
}

// ---- the sounds -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The bass drum: low and long enough to own the bottom octave, under a bass that sits above it.
const BOOM: Drum = Drum {
    tone_hz: 54.0,
    tone_t60: 0.36,
    sweep: 3.0,
    sweep_time: 0.014,
    drive: 2.6,
    click: 0.25,
    ..KICK,
}

/// The snare: fat, its wires ringing a third of a second.
const FAT: Drum = Drum {
    tone_hz: 180.0,
    tone: 0.9,
    noise: 1.5,
    band_hz: 1700.0,
    top_hz: 8000.0,
    noise_t60: 0.32,
    click: 0.25,
    ..SNARE,
}

/// Two toms: a skin with no wires, a little above and a little below the bass.
const TOM_HIGH: Drum = Drum {
    tone_hz: 150.0,
    tone: 1.0,
    tone_t60: 0.3,
    sweep: 0.5,
    sweep_time: 0.03,
    drive: 1.5,
    thump: 0.5,
    click: 0.1,
    range_db: 16.0,
}
const TOM_LOW: Drum = Drum { tone_hz: 100.0, tone_t60: 0.38, ..TOM_HIGH }

/// A shaker: a short breath of high noise, softer and duller when it is struck softly.
const SHAKER: Drum = Drum {
    noise: 1.0,
    band_hz: 7200.0,
    band_q: 1.1,
    cut_hz: 4500.0,
    noise_t60: 0.06,
    range_db: 18.0,
    soft_hz: 5000.0,
    ring_touch: 0.4,
}

/// A ride cymbal, struck on every beat of the chorus: a wash.
const RIDE: Drum = Drum {
    metal_tune: 1.3,
    noise: 0.2,
    band_hz: 6500.0,
    band_q: 0.5,
    cut_hz: 3500.0,
    noise_t60: 1.0,
    ring_touch: 0.1,
    range_db: 16.0,
    ..HAT,
}

/// A crash cymbal: metal and noise together, wide open, two seconds long.
const CRASH: Drum = Drum {
    metal: 0.8,
    metal_tune: 1.15,
    noise: 0.9,
    band_hz: 6000.0,
    band_q: 0.4,
    cut_hz: 2600.0,
    noise_t60: 2.0,
    ring_touch: 0.0,
    ..HAT,
}

/// The bass's lower layer: the sub, held (it doesn't die away like a drum machine's).
const DEEP: Patch = Patch {
    glide: 0.08,
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.006, decay: 1.2, sustain: 0.7, release: 0.1 },
    drive: 2.4,
    ..SUB,
}

/// The bass's upper layer, an octave over it: a triangle and a sine with a little sawtooth
/// under a low filter, so the line is there on a small speaker.
const ROUND: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.25,
    triangle: 0.6,
    sine: 0.5,
    glide: 0.08,
    cutoff: 450.0,
    open: 1.6,
    q: 0.8,
    follow: 0.3,
    touch: 0.5,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.004, decay: 0.3, sustain: 0.4, release: 0.1 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.005, decay: 0.9, sustain: 0.65, release: 0.1 },
    drive: 1.4,
    lean: 0.2,
    range_db: 10.0,
    voices: 1,
    level: 0.5,
}

/// The plucked figure: a string picked cleanly, bright for a moment and then round, each note
/// ringing into the next.
const PICKED: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.35,
    pulse: 0.2,
    width: 0.4,
    triangle: 0.35,
    spread: 5.0,
    wide: 0.5,
    cutoff: 520.0,
    open: 3.2,
    q: 1.0,
    follow: 0.5,
    touch: 1.0,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.001, decay: 0.22, sustain: 0.1, release: 0.3 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.002, decay: 0.8, sustain: 0.15, release: 0.4 },
    range_db: 14.0,
    level: 0.3,
}

/// The wall: sawtooths and a pulse a sixth of a semitone apart, driven hard and held, as an
/// overdriven guitar holds a chord of roots and fifths.
const WALL: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.6,
    pulse: 0.35,
    width: 0.45,
    spread: 16.0,
    wide: 0.3,
    cutoff: 3400.0,
    open: 1.0,
    q: 0.8,
    follow: 0.3,
    touch: 0.3,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.004, decay: 0.3, sustain: 0.8, release: 0.1 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.004, decay: 0.3, sustain: 0.9, release: 0.07 },
    drive: 4.0,
    lean: 0.3,
    range_db: 8.0,
    voices: 6,
    level: 0.3,
}

/// The voices: the pad made to sound sung, a triangle over a sawtooth with a late vibrato,
/// coming in over a fifth of a second.
const CHOIR: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.3,
    triangle: 0.5,
    spread: 10.0,
    wide: 0.9,
    vibrato: 8.0,
    vibrato_hz: 5.0,
    vibrato_wake: 0.4,
    cutoff: 900.0,
    open: 1.2,
    q: 0.8,
    follow: 0.4,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.25, decay: 1.0, sustain: 0.7, release: 0.5 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.18, decay: 0.8, sustain: 0.85, release: 0.5 },
    ..PAD,
}

/// The lead: the sung lead, a little brighter and quicker to speak.
const SUNG: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.35,
    triangle: 0.55,
    spread: 6.0,
    wide: 0.4,
    glide: 0.06,
    vibrato: 11.0,
    vibrato_hz: 5.4,
    vibrato_wake: 0.3,
    cutoff: 950.0,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.008, decay: 0.4, sustain: 0.5, release: 0.25 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.008, decay: 0.6, sustain: 0.85, release: 0.18 },
    drive: 0.8,
    ..LEAD,
}

/// The piano that twinkles: the electric piano with more of its bell, played high and softly.
const BELL: Tine = Tine { bell: 0.16, tremolo: 0.5, top_hz: 9000.0, ..SUITCASE }

// ---- the drums --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// A drum's part: the bars' text.
fn drum(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Pattern {
    pattern(name, four(), lines)
}

fn silent(bars: u32) -> Pattern {
    tacet(four(), bars: bars)
}

/// The verse: a soft bass drum on one. The chorus, in half time: the bass drum every dotted
/// quarter (with every second group of the figure), the snare on three.
fn kick() -> Pattern {
    let soft = drum("kick", ["o... .... .... ...."])
    let chorus = drum(
        "kick",
        [
            "X... ..x. .... x... | X... ..x. .... x... | X... ..x. .... x... | X... ..x. .... .... |",
            "X... ..x. .... x... | X... ..x. .... x... | X... ..x. .... x... | X... ..x. .... x... |",
        ],
    )
    silent(2)
        .then(soft.times(6))
        .then(chorus.clone())
        .then(soft.times(6))
        .then(chorus)
        .then(silent(2))
}

fn snare() -> Pattern {
    let chorus = drum("snare", [".... .... X... ...."]).times(8)
    silent(8).then(chorus.clone()).then(silent(6)).then(chorus).then(silent(2))
}

/// The toms: a fill in the tune's rest, in the fourth bar of each chorus (bars 12 and 26). The
/// choruses themselves come in with no fill.
fn tom_low() -> Pattern {
    let fill = drum("tom low", [".... .... .... xx.."])
    silent(11).then(fill.clone()).then(silent(13)).then(fill).then(silent(6))
}

fn tom_high() -> Pattern {
    let fill = drum("tom high", [".... .... ..xx ...."])
    silent(11).then(fill.clone()).then(silent(13)).then(fill).then(silent(6))
}

/// A rim on two and four in the verses; it stops with the figure, half a bar before each
/// chorus.
fn rim() -> Pattern {
    let back = drum("rim", [".... x... .... x..."])
    let half = drum("rim", [".... x... .... ...."])
    silent(4)
        .then(back.times(3))
        .then(half.clone())
        .then(silent(8))
        .then(back.times(5))
        .then(half)
        .then(silent(10))
}

/// A shaker on the eighths in the verses.
fn shaker() -> Pattern {
    let eighths = drum("shaker", ["x.o. x.o. x.o. x.o."])
    let half = drum("shaker", ["x.o. x.o. .... ...."])
    silent(4)
        .then(eighths.times(3))
        .then(half.clone())
        .then(silent(8))
        .then(eighths.times(5))
        .then(half)
        .then(silent(10))
}

/// The ride on every beat of the choruses.
fn ride() -> Pattern {
    let wash = drum("ride", ["X... x... x... x..."])
    silent(8).then(wash.times(8)).then(silent(6)).then(wash.times(8)).then(silent(2))
}

/// A crash where each chorus starts, and halfway through it.
fn crash() -> Pattern {
    let one = drum("crash", ["X... .... .... ...."])
    silent(8)
        .then(one.clone())
        .then(silent(3))
        .then(one.clone())
        .then(silent(9))
        .then(one.clone())
        .then(silent(3))
        .then(one)
        .then(silent(5))
}

// ---- the parts written as notes ---------------------------------------------------------------

fn part(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Score {
    score(TITLE, four()).voice(name, lines)
}

/// `bars` bars of rest for the part `name`.
fn rests(name: Text, bars: u32) -> Score {
    var s = part(name, ["r/1 |"])
    for _ in 1..bars {
        s = take s.then(part(name, ["r/1 |"]))
    }
    s
}

// The figure. A bar of it is sixteen sixteenths in groups of three, three, three, three, two
// and two: a top note, then B and E under it, the same two every time. Only the top note
// changes, one to a bar: B, A, G, F♯.
const FLOW_B: Text = "b4/16 !mp b3 e3 b4 b3 e3 b4 b3 e3 b4 b3 e3 b4 b3 b4 b3 |"
const FLOW_A: Text = "a4/16 b3 e3 a4 b3 e3 a4 b3 e3 a4 b3 e3 a4 b3 a4 b3 |"
const FLOW_G: Text = "g4/16 b3 e3 g4 b3 e3 g4 b3 e3 g4 b3 e3 g4 b3 g4 b3 |"
const FLOW_F: Text = "f#4/16 b3 e3 f#4 b3 e3 f#4 b3 e3 f#4 b3 e3 f#4 b3 f#4 b3 |"
/// Half a bar of it, and then nothing, for the lead to come in alone: on F♯ (bar 8) and on A
/// (bar 22).
const FLOW_F_STOPS: Text = "f#4/16 b3 e3 f#4 b3 e3 f#4 b3 r/2 |"
const FLOW_A_STOPS: Text = "a4/16 b3 e3 a4 b3 e3 a4 b3 r/2 |"
/// The last bar: the top note is E at last, and it stops on E and B.
const FLOW_HOME: Text = "e4/16 !mp b3 e3 e4 b3 e3 e4 b3 <e3 b3 e4>/2 !tenuto |"

/// The plucked figure: alone at the start, under both verses, and again at the end.
fn flow() -> Score {
    part("flow", [FLOW_B, FLOW_A, FLOW_G, FLOW_F, FLOW_B, FLOW_A, FLOW_G, FLOW_F_STOPS])
        .then(rests("flow", bars: 8))
        .then(part("flow", [FLOW_B, FLOW_A, FLOW_G, FLOW_F, FLOW_B, FLOW_A_STOPS]))
        .then(rests("flow", bars: 8))
        .then(part("flow", [FLOW_B, FLOW_HOME]))
}

// The chorus's chords, a bar each: C, D, E minor, E minor, C, D, C, D. It never ends on its own
// home chord: the bar after it does.
//
// The bass, in two layers an octave apart (`BASS_` the lower, `ROUND_` the upper). In the verses
// only the upper one plays, holding each root very softly. In the choruses both strike the
// figure's own rhythm, three, three, three, three, two, two, on the root: the figure, made
// heavy.
const BASS_CHORUS: Text = "c2/8. !f c2 c2 c2 c2/8 c2 | d2/8. d2 d2 d2 d2/8 d2 | e1/8. e1 e1 e1 e1/8 e1 | e1/8. e1 e1 e1 e1/8 e1 | c2/8. c2 c2 c2 c2/8 c2 | d2/8. d2 d2 d2 d2/8 d2 | c2/8. c2 c2 c2 c2/8 c2 | d2/8. d2 d2 d2 d2/8 d2 |"
const ROUND_CHORUS: Text = "c3/8. !f c3 c3 c3 c3/8 c3 | d3/8. d3 d3 d3 d3/8 d3 | e2/8. e2 e2 e2 e2/8 e2 | e2/8. e2 e2 e2 e2/8 e2 | c3/8. c3 c3 c3 c3/8 c3 | d3/8. d3 d3 d3 d3/8 d3 | c3/8. c3 c3 c3 c3/8 c3 | d3/8. d3 d3 d3 d3/8 d3 |"

fn bass() -> Score {
    rests("bass", bars: 8)
        .then(part("bass", [BASS_CHORUS]))
        .then(rests("bass", bars: 6))
        .then(part("bass", [BASS_CHORUS, "e2/1~ !p | e2/1 |"]))
}

fn round() -> Score {
    part("round", ["r/1 | r/1 | c3/1 !pp | c3/1 | e3/1 | e3/1 | c3/1 | c3/2 r/2 |", ROUND_CHORUS])
        .then(part("round", ["e3/1 !pp | e3/1 | c3/1 | c3/1 | e3/1 | e3/2 r/2 |", ROUND_CHORUS]))
        .then(part("round", ["e3/1~ !p | e3/1 |"]))
}

// The wall, in two layers to either side. On the left each chord's root, fifth and octave,
// low, striking the figure's rhythm with the bass. On the right its three notes, higher, held
// a bar.
const WALL_LOW: Text = "<c3 g3 c4>/8. !f <c3 g3 c4> <c3 g3 c4> <c3 g3 c4> <c3 g3 c4>/8 <c3 g3 c4> | <d3 a3 d4>/8. <d3 a3 d4> <d3 a3 d4> <d3 a3 d4> <d3 a3 d4>/8 <d3 a3 d4> | <e2 b2 e3>/8. <e2 b2 e3> <e2 b2 e3> <e2 b2 e3> <e2 b2 e3>/8 <e2 b2 e3> | <e2 b2 e3>/8. <e2 b2 e3> <e2 b2 e3> <e2 b2 e3> <e2 b2 e3>/8 <e2 b2 e3> | <c3 g3 c4>/8. <c3 g3 c4> <c3 g3 c4> <c3 g3 c4> <c3 g3 c4>/8 <c3 g3 c4> | <d3 a3 d4>/8. <d3 a3 d4> <d3 a3 d4> <d3 a3 d4> <d3 a3 d4>/8 <d3 a3 d4> | <c3 g3 c4>/8. <c3 g3 c4> <c3 g3 c4> <c3 g3 c4> <c3 g3 c4>/8 <c3 g3 c4> | <d3 a3 d4>/8. <d3 a3 d4> <d3 a3 d4> <d3 a3 d4> <d3 a3 d4>/8 <d3 a3 d4> |"
const WALL_HIGH: Text = "<g3 c4 e4>/1 !f !tenuto | <a3 d4 f#4>/1 !tenuto | <b3 e4 g4>/1~ !tenuto | <b3 e4 g4>/1 | <g3 c4 e4>/1 !tenuto | <a3 d4 f#4>/1 !tenuto | <g3 c4 e4>/1 !tenuto | <a3 d4 f#4>/1 !tenuto |"

/// One side of the wall: silent in the verses, `chorus` in both choruses.
fn wall(name: Text, chorus: Text) -> Score {
    rests(name, bars: 8)
        .then(part(name, [chorus]))
        .then(rests(name, bars: 6))
        .then(part(name, [chorus]))
        .then(rests(name, bars: 2))
}

/// The voices. In the verses, E and B, the two notes the figure never leaves, very softly. In
/// the choruses, each chord's three notes, high.
fn choir() -> Score {
    let high: Text = "<e5 g5 c6>/1 !mf | <f#5 a5 d6>/1 | <e5 g5 b5>/1~ | <e5 g5 b5>/1 | <e5 g5 c6>/1 | <f#5 a5 d6>/1 | <e5 g5 c6>/1 | <f#5 a5 d6>/1 |"
    rests("choir", bars: 4)
        .then(part("choir", ["<e4 b4>/1~ !pp | <e4 b4>/1~ | <e4 b4>/1~ | <e4 b4>/2 r/2 |"]))
        .then(part("choir", [high]))
        .then(
            part(
                "choir",
                ["<e4 b4>/1~ !p | <e4 b4>/1~ | <e4 b4>/1~ | <e4 b4>/1~ | <e4 b4>/1~ | <e4 b4>/1 |"],
            ),
        )
        .then(part("choir", [high]))
        .then(part("choir", ["<e4 b4>/1~ !mp | <e4 b4>/1 |"]))
}

// The tune. Each note is sung and then touched again just before the next (a dotted quarter and
// an eighth): B with C over it, the same a step lower, then G, F♯ and home to E a push early.
// The second half starts the same, leaps to the high E, its one highest note, and comes down.
// The first chorus stops on B over the D chord and holds it across the bar line, where the
// verse's E minor arrives under it and the figure takes the B up: the cut is the resolution.
// The second walks on down the scale, and its last step, F♯ to E, lands as the last E minor
// does.
const TUNE_STARTS: Text = "b4/4. !f b4/8 c5/4. ( b4/8 ) | a4/4. a4/8 b4/4. ( a4/8 ) | g4/4. g4/8 f#4/4. ( e4/8~ | e4/2 ) r/2 | b4/4. b4/8 c5/4. ( b4/8 ) | a4/4. a4/8 b4/4. ( a4/8 ) |"
const TUNE_HANGS: Text = "e5/4. e5/8 d5/2 | c5/4. c5/8 b4/2~ | b4/4 r/2. |"
const TUNE_LANDS: Text = "e5/4. e5/8 d5/4. ( c5/8 ) | b4/4. a4/8 g4/4 ( f#4/4 | e4/1 ) |"
/// Four eighths up the scale, alone, into the tune's first note.
const PICKUP: Text = "r/2 e4/8 !mf f#4/8 g4/8 a4/8 |"

/// The lead: the pickup alone, then the tune, twice.
fn lead() -> Score {
    rests("lead", bars: 7)
        .then(part("lead", [PICKUP, TUNE_STARTS, TUNE_HANGS]))
        .then(rests("lead", bars: 4))
        .then(part("lead", [PICKUP, TUNE_STARTS, TUNE_LANDS]))
        .then(rests("lead", bars: 1))
}

/// A second voice a third over the tune, in the second half of each chorus only.
fn harmony() -> Score {
    let starts: Text = "d5/4. !mf d5/8 e5/4. ( d5/8 ) | c5/4. c5/8 d5/4. ( c5/8 ) |"
    rests("harmony", bars: 12)
        .then(part("harmony", [starts, "g5/4. g5/8 f#5/2 | e5/4. e5/8 d5/2~ | d5/4 r/2. |"]))
        .then(rests("harmony", bars: 9))
        .then(
            part(
                "harmony",
                [starts, "g5/4. g5/8 f#5/4. ( e5/8 ) | d5/4. c5/8 b4/4 ( a4/4 | g4/1 ) |"],
            ),
        )
        .then(rests("harmony", bars: 1))
}

/// The piano's high notes, a few to a bar, in the verses and at the end: each is a note of the
/// chord under it.
fn twinkle() -> Score {
    rests("twinkle", bars: 4)
        .then(
            part(
                "twinkle",
                ["r/2 r/8 b5/8 !p r/4 | r/4. e6/8~ e6/2 | r/2 g5/8 b5/8 r/4 | r/1 |"],
            ),
        )
        .then(rests("twinkle", bars: 8))
        .then(
            part(
                "twinkle",
                [
                    "r/4. b5/8~ !p b5/2 | r/2 r/8 e6/8 r/4 | r/4 g5/8 b5/8~ b5/2 | r/2. e6/4 |",
                    "r/4. b5/8~ b5/2 | r/1 |",
                ],
            ),
        )
        .then(rests("twinkle", bars: 8))
        .then(part("twinkle", ["r/2 r/8 b5/8 !p r/4 | r/2 e6/2 |"]))
}

/// The cello: the figure's top notes an octave down, a bar each, in the second verse, swelling
/// through its last two bars; in the second chorus the roots; E to the end.
fn cello() -> Score {
    rests("cello", bars: 16)
        .then(
            part(
                "cello",
                ["b3/1 !p ( | a3/1 | g3/1 | f#3/1 ) | b3/2 !mp b3/2 !mf | a3/2 !f a3/2 !ff |"],
            ),
        )
        .then(part("cello", ["c3/1 !f | d3/1 | e3/1~ | e3/1 | c3/1 | d3/1 | c3/1 | d3/1 |"]))
        .then(part("cello", ["e3/1~ !mp | e3/1 |"]))
}

/// The viola: E, swelling, into the second chorus; then each chord's third; B to the end.
fn viola() -> Score {
    rests("viola", bars: 20)
        .then(part("viola", ["e4/2 !p e4/2 !mp | e4/2 !mf e4/4 !f e4/4 !ff |"]))
        .then(part("viola", ["e4/1 !f | f#4/1 | g4/1~ | g4/1 | e4/1 | f#4/1 | e4/1 | f#4/1 |"]))
        .then(part("viola", ["b3/1~ !mp | b3/1 |"]))
}

/// The violin: B, swelling, into the second chorus; then the tune an octave over the lead, to
/// its last E, which it holds to the end.
fn violin() -> Score {
    rests("violin", bars: 20)
        .then(part("violin", ["b4/2 !p b4/2 !mp | b4/2 !mf b4/4 !f b4/4 !ff |"]))
        .then(
            part(
                "violin",
                [
                    "b5/4. !f b5/8 c6/4. ( b5/8 ) | a5/4. a5/8 b5/4. ( a5/8 ) | g5/4. g5/8 f#5/4. ( e5/8~ | e5/2 ) r/2 |",
                    "b5/4. b5/8 c6/4. ( b5/8 ) | a5/4. a5/8 b5/4. ( a5/8 ) | e6/4. e6/8 d6/4. ( c6/8 ) |",
                    "b5/4. a5/8 g5/4 ( f#5/4 | e5/1~ !mp | e5/1 ) |",
                ],
            ),
        )
}

/// A score as a player with `taste` plays it.
fn played(s: Score, taste: Taste) -> Performance {
    swung(perform(s, taste, [Mark::Hold { at: bar(1), by: 1.0 }; 0]), Feel {})
}

// ---- the session ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The whole track, ready to play.
pub fn build() -> Session {
    var s = session(
        TEMPO,
        Master {
            gain: 4.0,
            glue_db: -16.0,
            glue: 0.35,
            makeup: 5.0,
            warmth: 1.0,
            ceiling: -1.0,
            room_time: 1.4,
            room_size: 1.6,
            room_db: -4.0,
            echo_beats: 0.75,
            echo_again: 0.4,
            echo_db: -5.0,
            duck_time: 0.16,
        },
    )
    s.drum(
        "kick",
        BOOM,
        struck(kick(), TEMPO, Feel { loose: 0.001, uneven: 0.03, seed: 1 }, key: 36),
        Strip { gain: -1.0, room: 0.05 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "snare",
        FAT,
        struck(snare(), TEMPO, Feel { late: 0.006, loose: 0.002, uneven: 0.06, seed: 2 }, key: 38),
        Strip { gain: -3.0, low_cut: 100.0, drive: 1.4, room: 0.35 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "tom low",
        TOM_LOW,
        struck(tom_low(), TEMPO, Feel { loose: 0.002, uneven: 0.06, seed: 3 }, key: 43),
        Strip { gain: -5.0, pan: 0.3, low_cut: 70.0, room: 0.3 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "tom high",
        TOM_HIGH,
        struck(tom_high(), TEMPO, Feel { loose: 0.002, uneven: 0.06, seed: 4 }, key: 47),
        Strip { gain: -5.0, pan: -0.3, low_cut: 90.0, room: 0.3 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "rim",
        RIM,
        struck(rim(), TEMPO, Feel { late: 0.006, loose: 0.003, uneven: 0.08, seed: 5 }, key: 37),
        Strip { gain: -9.0, pan: -0.25, room: 0.4 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "shaker",
        SHAKER,
        struck(
            shaker(),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { late: -0.003, loose: 0.003, uneven: 0.18, seed: 6 },
            key: 70,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -15.0, pan: 0.4, low_cut: 2000.0, room: 0.2 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "ride",
        RIDE,
        struck(ride(), TEMPO, Feel { loose: 0.003, uneven: 0.1, seed: 7 }, key: 51),
        Strip { gain: -7.0, pan: -0.35, room: 0.2 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "crash",
        CRASH,
        struck(crash(), TEMPO, Feel { seed: 8 }, key: 49),
        Strip { gain: -14.0, pan: 0.25, room: 0.3 },
    )
    s.key("kick")
    s.synth(
        "bass",
        DEEP,
        played(bass(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.05 }),
        Strip { gain: -7.0, high_cut: 1500.0, duck: 4.0 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "round",
        ROUND,
        played(round(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.06 }),
        Strip { gain: -9.0, low_cut: 100.0, high_cut: 2500.0, duck: 3.0 },
    )
    // The figure: its top notes a little harder than the two under them, and an echo a dotted
    // eighth behind.
    s.synth(
        "flow",
        PICKED,
        played(
            flow(),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.0, high_loud: 0.25, jitter_velocity: 0.06, seed: 9 },
        ),
        Strip { gain: -6.0, pan: -0.15, low_cut: 120.0, room: 0.3, echo: 0.3 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "wall left",
        WALL,
        played(
            wall("wall left", WALL_LOW),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.2, roll: 0.008, seed: 10 },
        ),
        Strip { gain: 0.0, pan: -0.75, low_cut: 70.0, high_cut: 8000.0, room: 0.2, duck: 1.5 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "wall right",
        Patch { spread: 22.0, ..WALL },
        played(
            wall("wall right", WALL_HIGH),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.2, roll: 0.012, seed: 11 },
        ),
        Strip { gain: -1.0, pan: 0.75, low_cut: 140.0, high_cut: 8000.0, room: 0.2, duck: 1.5 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "choir",
        CHOIR,
        played(choir(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.02 }),
        Strip { gain: -9.0, low_cut: 200.0, high_cut: 7000.0, room: 0.5 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "lead",
        SUNG,
        played(
            lead(),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, legato: 0.05, detache: 0.08, jitter_velocity: 0.04, seed: 12 },
        ),
        Strip { gain: -3.0, low_cut: 200.0, room: 0.3, echo: 0.2 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "harmony",
        Patch { vibrato: 8.0, ..SUNG },
        played(
            harmony(),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, legato: 0.05, detache: 0.08, jitter_velocity: 0.04, seed: 14 },
        ),
        Strip { gain: -8.0, pan: 0.3, low_cut: 250.0, room: 0.35, echo: 0.2 },
    )
    s.tine(
        "twinkle",
        BELL,
        played(twinkle(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.02, jitter_velocity: 0.08, seed: 13 }),
        Strip { gain: -10.0, pan: 0.35, low_cut: 400.0, room: 0.45, echo: 0.4 },
    )
    let strings = Taste { tempo: TEMPO, legato: 0.04, detache: 0.03 }
    let cello_part = cello()
    let cello_played = played(cello_part, strings)
    s.bowed(
        "cello",
        CELLO,
        bowings(cello_part, cello_played, 0, -22.0),
        Strip { gain: -8.0, pan: 0.2, low_cut: 80.0, room: 0.4 },
    )
    let viola_part = viola()
    let viola_played = played(viola_part, strings)
    s.bowed(
        "viola",
        VIOLA,
        bowings(viola_part, viola_played, 0, -22.0),
        Strip { gain: -10.0, pan: -0.2, low_cut: 120.0, room: 0.45 },
    )
    let violin_part = violin()
    let violin_played = played(violin_part, strings)
    s.bowed(
        "violin",
        VIOLIN,
        bowings(violin_part, violin_played, 0, -22.0),
        Strip { gain: -11.0, pan: -0.4, low_cut: 180.0, room: 0.45 },
    )
    s
}
